# paq8-N0.idx -- the bit-history state machine, as a construction rule.
#
# paq8-T0/T1.idx hold the state machine as 1012 tabulated bytes.  This file
# holds the same machine as the seven numbers it can be DERIVED from, using
# fxcmv1's StateTable generator (see statetable.inc).  Which of the two the
# build uses is PAQ_STATE_TABLE_GEN, defaulting to this one.
#
# A state is a pair (x,y) = (zeros seen, ones seen), bounded and quantised:
#
#   B0..B4  the largest x allowed at y = 0,1,2,3,4.  y is capped at 4, so the
#           machine tracks a long run of one bit and at most four of the other
#           -- the paq8 asymmetry, here as a parameter rather than a fact.
#   B5      the doubling threshold: a cell with y>0 and x+y < B5 is worth TWO
#           state numbers instead of one, which is how the low-count region
#           buys finer resolution than the tail.
#   MDC     maximum discount: when the opposite bit arrives the majority count
#           collapses to min(x, MDC-1).  This is what keeps a long run one step
#           away from reachable states instead of stranding it.
#
# Six sets ship in fxcmv1, one per context-map family.  Measured on book1 at
# level 7, whole archive, each at the CM_DECAY_STEP that matches ITS OWN state
# numbering (see below), against the tabulated table's 191980 at its own best
# step:
#
#     set   B0 B1 B2 B3 B4 B5 MDC   step   book1
#     STA1  28 28 31 29 23  4  17     4    196385
#     STA2  32 28 31 28 21  5   6     8    192825
#     STA4  31 27 30 27 24  4  27    10    191729
#     STA5  33 31 31 24 20  4  33     6    191572   <- seeded below
#     STA6  28 29 30 30 23  3  22     6    196714
#     STA7  28 29 33 23 23  6  14     2    196795
#
# STA5 is the best of the six and beats the tabulated table by 408 bytes
# (-0.21%).  The tabulated table was checked at steps 4, 6 and 8 for the same
# comparison and is best at its shipped 4, so this is not a matter of one side
# being tuned and the other not.
#
# CM_DECAY_STEP HAS TO MOVE WITH THIS FILE
#
# That is the whole reason the first measurements looked bad -- every set came
# out 500 to 5000 bytes WORSE until the step was matched.  paq8hpc's decay does
# `ns -= CM_DECAY_STEP` to step a saturated state back by one observation, and
# how many state numbers "one observation" spans is a property of the state
# NUMBERING: the tabulated machine puts 4 states on each x+y level, STA5 puts
# 6, STA4 puts 10, STA7 puts 2.  A step of 4 against a 6-wide level lands
# mid-level, on a state with a different x/y balance rather than one fewer
# observation.  STA5 alone goes 195653 -> 191572 on that one change.
#
# So CM_DECAY_STEP in paq8-G0.idx is now 6, and anyone reseeding this file must
# re-measure it.  B5 is the parameter that moves the level width most (it is
# the doubling threshold), so a swept B5 silently invalidates the step.
#
# Widths are six bits.  The b's live in 20..35 across all six sets and the
# lattice is 64 wide, so six bits covers the range the design admits; MDC's
# shipped values span 6..33.  Both are clamped at the point of use, which for
# B is not decoration: next_state() walks down the lattice until it finds a
# cell that exists, so a B admitting no states at all would walk x negative.

Prefix N0
Debug 1
Const 0

Number B0, 1, 0!100001
Number B1, 1, 0!011111
Number B2, 1, 0!011111
Number B3, 1, 0!011000
Number B4, 1, 0!010100
Number B5, 1, 0!000100
Number MDC,1, 0!100001
